{\pard\sa120\qc\f1\fs52\b\cf1 Lite Simple Rust Browser\b0\par}
{\pard\sa360\qc\f1\fs26\i\cf2 A light, simple web browser written in Rust\i0\par}
{\pard\sa200\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\brsp1\brdrcf3\par}
{\pard\sb280\sa100\keepn\f1\fs32\b\cf1 Overview\b0\par}
{\pard\sa140\sl300\slmult1\f1\fs22 Lite Simple Rust Browser (internal name: Kumo) is a web browser written from scratch in Rust with low memory use as its first goal. It parses HTML and CSS, lays out, paints, fetches over the network and runs JavaScript with its own engine, so it stays light however many tabs you open.\par}
{\pard\sb280\sa100\keepn\f1\fs32\b\cf1 Features\b0\par}
{\pard\fi-300\li520\sa80\sl290\slmult1\f1\fs22 \u8226?\tab {\b Low memory} About 22 MB for a blank tab, about 65 MB for one Wikipedia article and about 185 MB for ten tabs (measured on a release build). Background tabs are frozen and discarded automatically to stay within a memory budget.\par}
{\pard\fi-300\li520\sa80\sl290\slmult1\f1\fs22 \u8226?\tab {\b Three processes} Browser, Content and Network run as separate processes, so the window stays responsive even when a page is heavy. If the Content process stops, it is restarted automatically.\par}
{\pard\fi-300\li520\sa80\sl290\slmult1\f1\fs22 \u8226?\tab {\b JavaScript} Runs the DOM, events, timers, fetch and more on the Boa engine, with a script budget that follows the load level.\par}
{\pard\fi-300\li520\sa80\sl290\slmult1\f1\fs22 \u8226?\tab {\b Load levels 1-5} From "Minimal" (HTML and inline CSS only) to "Maximum". Image loading can be switched on or off separately.\par}
{\pard\fi-300\li520\sa80\sl290\slmult1\f1\fs22 \u8226?\tab {\b Password manager} Asks to save when you sign in and fills it in next time on the same site. Passwords are encrypted, and the key is kept in the Windows Credential Manager.\par}
{\pard\fi-300\li520\sa80\sl290\slmult1\f1\fs22 \u8226?\tab {\b Bookmarks and home page} Ctrl+D to add, Ctrl+B for the list. Choose your home page in Settings.\par}
{\pard\fi-300\li520\sa80\sl290\slmult1\f1\fs22 \u8226?\tab {\b History and downloads} Ctrl+H for your browsing history (delete one entry or clear all), Ctrl+J for the download list. Opening a link to a file saves it to your Downloads folder without leaving the page, with live progress.\par}
{\pard\fi-300\li520\sa80\sl290\slmult1\f1\fs22 \u8226?\tab {\b Five display languages} Japanese, English, Simplified Chinese, Korean and Spanish. The browser's own screens (settings, new tab, error pages) switch language.\par}
{\pard\fi-300\li520\sa80\sl290\slmult1\f1\fs22 \u8226?\tab {\b Content blocking} Block ads and other unwanted requests with filter lists.\par}
{\pard\sb280\sa100\keepn\f1\fs32\b\cf1 Getting started\b0\par}
{\pard\fi-300\li520\sa80\sl290\slmult1\f1\fs22 \u8226?\tab A new tab opens at startup. Type a URL or something to search for in the box at the top (Ctrl+L).\par}
{\pard\fi-300\li520\sa80\sl290\slmult1\f1\fs22 \u8226?\tab Main keys: Ctrl+T (new tab), Ctrl+W (close), Alt+Left (back), Alt+Home (home), Ctrl+click (open in a background tab).\par}
{\pard\fi-300\li520\sa80\sl290\slmult1\f1\fs22 \u8226?\tab See about:settings for settings, about:passwords for saved passwords and about:memory for memory use.\par}
{\pard\fi-300\li520\sa80\sl290\slmult1\f1\fs22 \u8226?\tab From the command line: kumo.exe https://example.com/  (use --help for the options).\par}
{\pard\sb280\sa100\keepn\f1\fs32\b\cf1 Current limitations\b0\par}
{\pard\sa140\sl300\slmult1\f1\fs22 This is a work in progress, so not every site renders perfectly. ES modules, iframes, canvas, GPU rendering and inline SVG are not supported yet. The display language at startup is always Japanese, and showing a saved password does not require a master password.\par}
{\pard\sb280\sa100\keepn\f1\fs32\b\cf1 Requirements and license\b0\par}
{\pard\sa140\sl300\slmult1\f1\fs22 Windows 11 (64-bit). Use the installer, or just unzip the package. History and settings are stored in %LOCALAPPDATA%\\Kumo. Licensed under your choice of MIT or Apache-2.0.\par}
